[statement]
A header's checksum is the sum of its bytes as unsigned numbers. Some
historical writers summed them as signed numbers, which differs wherever a
header holds a byte above 0x7f, as this one's name does. Every reference
reader accepts either sum, as GNU tar documents, and so does ferrotape.

[archive]
header name="caf\xe9" checksum=signed
data "x\n"
end

